aidi","from_t":1888.4234972677596,"to_t":1913.7698630136986,"title":"Sultan of Oman","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Faisal bin Turki Al Busaidi"},{"qid":"Q842","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q107970099","value_label":"Muhammed al-Fallah","from_t":1406,"to_t":1435,"title":"Sultan of Oman","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Muhammed al-Fallah"},{"qid":"Q842","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q114528647","value_label":"Muhammad bin Ismail","from_t":1500,"to_t":1501,"title":"Sultan of Oman","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Muhammad bin Ismail"},{"qid":"Q842","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q114529580","value_label":"Taamir al Barakat","from_t":1596,"to_t":1615,"title":"Sultan of Oman","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Taamir al Barakat"},{"qid":"Q842","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q57331","value_label":"Qaboos bin Said Al Said","from_t":1970.5561643835617,"to_t":2020.0245901639344,"title":"Sultan of Oman","property":"P39","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Qaboos bin Said Al Said"},{"qid":"Q842","kind":"flag","value_qid":"Q165550","value_label":"Flag of Oman.svg","from_t":1995.3123287671233,"to_t":null,"title":"flag of Oman","property":"P163","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"flag of Oman"}],"people":{"Q12250314":{"label":"Haitham bin Tarik Al Said","description":"Sultan of Oman since 2020 (born 1955)","enwiki":"Haitham bin Tariq","summary":"Haitham bin Tariq Al Said (born 11 October 1955) is Sultan and Prime Minister of Oman. He acceded to the throne in 2020 following the death of his cousin, Sultan Qaboos bin Said, becoming the fifteenth ruler of the Al Bu Said dynasty, which has ruled Oman since the mid-eighteenth century. \nHaitham was born in Muscat to Sayyid Tariq bin Taimur, an uncle of Sultan Qaboos who served as his first Prime Minister from 1970 to 1972. He received his primary education at Al Saidiya School in Muscat before continuing his secondary and university studies in the United Kingdom.","image":"Official portrait of Sultan Haitham bin Tariq (2021).jpg","birth":1955.7753424657535,"death":null},"Q879869":{"label":"Said bin Taimur Al Said","description":"Sultan of Muscat and Oman (1910-1972)","enwiki":"Said bin Taimur","summary":"Said bin Taimur (Arabic: سعيد بن تيمور; 13 August 1910 – 19 October 1972) was the 13th Sultan of Muscat and Oman from 10 February 1932 until he was deposed on 23 July 1970 by the British with the help of his son, Qaboos bin Said.\nHe was a member of the Al Bu Said dynasty who in 1932 became the Sultan of Muscat and Oman, succeeding his father, Sultan Taimur bin Feisal who had abdicated for financial reasons. The 21-year-old Said inherited an administration that was in debt. He consolidated power, with the help of the British, and regained control of the tribal interior, bringing together Muscat and Oman.","image":"Sultan Wayyid Said Bin Taimur Bin Faisal arriving in Wash. to repay visit made by Edmund Roberts (1832), who was appointed by Pres. Andrew Jackson to negotiate treaties with small nations of LCCN2016878033 (cropped).jpg","birth":1910.613698630137,"death":1972.7978142076502},"Q888278":{"label":"Taimur bin Faisal Al Said","description":"Sultan of Oman (1886-1965)","enwiki":"Taimur bin Feisal","summary":"Sultan Taimur bin Faisal bin Turki Al Said (Arabic: تيمور بن فيصل بن تركي; 1886 – 28 January 1965) was the Sultan of Muscat and Oman from 5 October 1913 to 10 February 1932.","image":"Taimur bin Feisal.png","birth":1886,"death":1965.0739726027398},"Q889847":{"label":"Faisal bin Turki Al Busaidi","description":"Sultan of Muscat and Oman (1864-1913)","enwiki":"Faisal bin Turki Al Busaidi","summary":"Sultan Faisal bin Turki bin Said Al Busaidi (Arabic: فيصل بن تركي بن سعيد البوسعيدي) (8 June 1864 – 4 October 1913) was the Sultan of Muscat and Oman from 4 June 1888 to 4 October 1913.","image":"Faysal bin Turki.jpg","birth":1864.4344262295083,"death":1913.7561643835616},"Q107970099":{"label":"Muhammed al-Fallah","description":null,"enwiki":null,"summary":null,"image":null,"birth":1378,"death":1435},"Q114528647":{"label":"Muhammad bin Ismail","description":"monarch","enwiki":null,"summary":null,"image":null,"birth":1481,"death":1548},"Q114529580":{"label":"Taamir al Barakat","description":"monarch","enwiki":null,"summary":null,"image":null,"birth":1558,"death":1615},"Q57331":{"label":"Qaboos bin Said Al Said","description":"sultan of Oman from 1970 to 2020 (1940–2020)","enwiki":"Qaboos bin Said","summary":"Qaboos bin Said Al Said (Arabic: قابوس بن سعيد آل سعيد, romanized: Qābūs ibn Saʿīd Āl Saʿīd, IPA: [qaː.buːs bin sa.ʕiːd ʔaːl sa.ʕiːd]; 18 November 1940 – 10 January 2020) was Sultan of Oman from 23 July 1970 until his death in 2020. A fifteenth-generation descendant of the founder of the Al Bu Said dynasty, he was the longest-serving leader in the Middle East and Arab world at the time of his death, having ruled for almost half a century.\nThe only son of Said bin Taimur, Sultan of Muscat and Oman, Qaboos was educated in Suffolk, England. After graduating from the Royal Military Academy Sandhurst, he served briefly in the British Army.","image":"Official portrait of Sultan Qaboos bin Said.jpg","birth":1940.879781420765,"death":2020.0245901639344}},"media":{"Flag of Muscat.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Flag_of_Muscat.svg/330px-Flag_of_Muscat.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Muscat.svg","author":null,"license":"Public domain"},"National emblem of Oman.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/National_emblem_of_Oman.svg/330px-National_emblem_of_Oman.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:National_emblem_of_Oman.svg","author":"See File history below for details.","license":"OGL-om 1.0"},"Flag of Oman.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki